{
  "schema": "fcpi.budget-policy/v1",
  "comment": "Provider spending (FIRECRAWL_PI_SPEC.md §10, §14, §15, §28.3; PI_BUDGET_POLICY_FILE). Every paid cap is zero until the owner approves one; PI_PAID_DISPATCH_ENABLED must also be true before a paid provider is called. Amounts are integers: micro-USD (1e-6 USD) or parser credits. A model or parser the policy does not list is refused; one without a rate card in effect is refused (fail closed). Fixture providers are unpaid and draw on their own categories, so the accounting runs end to end without money.",
  "notifyAtFraction": 0.8,
  "categories": {
    "llm": { "paid": true, "unit": "micro_usd", "caps": { "day": 0, "month": 0 } },
